**phase-080 complete.** Reproduced the finding exactly, wrote19 failing tests first, made them green, and ran the gates.

**Decision on the three SPEC.md lines, individually:** all three now run and print the documented value — nothing was struck.
- `set first to items at 0` → `1` (was `Unknown variable 'at'`)
- `set last to items at -1` → `3` (the last element, which is what `items[-1]` has always answered)
- `set count to length of items` → `3` (was `Unknown variable 'of'`)

**What changed**
- `src/parser.rs` +102 — `items at N` as a postfix on the existing `Expr::Index`; `length of X` as a primary producing the existing `length(X)` call. No new node, so one set of bounds, messages and bytecode behind both spellings. `at`/`length` stay ordinary names.
- `src/linter.rs` +35/−11 — `lint()` reports `Analysis error:` when `rb` could not run a file and the linter had nothing else to say (strictly additive; three existing linter findings untouched).
- `src/formatter.rs` +5/−3 — corrected a comment that claimed `object at index` is not syntax.
- `bootstrap/compiler.rb` +59 — the stage-2 compiler written in Redblue learned both forms, so the S3 fixed point still holds. No shim.
- SPEC.md, GRAMMAR.md, README (CI-pinned corpus count), 6 corpus programs, 19 tests, 8 of them `edge_*`.

**Gates**
| Gate | Result |
|---|---|
| `cargo fmt --all -- --check` | pass |
| `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` | pass, no `allow(` added |
| `cargo test --all-targets` | 1529 passed, 0 failed, 0 ignored |
| `./rbops/verify.sh phase-080` | **not run — `rbops/` does not exist in this checkout.** Not claimed as passing. |

Run by hand instead: `differential_test` (82 passed, both engines agree on all 367 programs), `bootstrap_selfhost_test` (20 passed, stage 2 and 3 byte-identical to stage 1 on every new corpus program), `bootstrap_ship_test` (16 passed), every `examples/*.rb` and `modules/*.rb` exits 0, and the three tools re-run on the original repro.

Two honest deviations, both in `REPORT.md`:
1. One existing fixture was corrected, no assertion changed: `function_parameter_is_not_a_false_positive` used `greet with "world"`, which is not Redblue syntax at all — it only lint-cleaned because lint stopped at the tree.
2. `rb lint` cannot report a run-time-only failure (unknown function, out-of-bounds); a linter reads the tree. Recorded in `FINDINGS.md §1` rather than papered over.
